{"name":"Shadow Taupe","hex":"#9c917f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"},{"term":"taupe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-grey colour, the colour of moleskin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taupe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"},{"title":"Taupe","blocks":[{"text":"Taupe is a dark gray-brown color. The word derives from the French noun taupe meaning \"mole\". The name originally referred only to the average color of the French mole, but beginning in the 1940s, its usage expanded to encompass a wider range of shades."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taupe","wikidata":"Q2307593"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/500px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wi